; The setter's leads. Winning 42 pp. 46-48 (S-0067-c, S-0069-b, S-0069-d,
; S-0070-c) and p. 51 (S-0074-c); played in Hands 15, 16, 28, 29 and 31 to 33
; (S-0048-b, S-0049-a, S-0051-a, S-0130-f, S-0131-a, S-0133-e, S-0133-i,
; S-0140-b, S-0143-b, S-0144-j).
; Rule, in our words: a setter on lead leads what can bring in count. When one
; more point sets the bid, he leads a double, count or not: the trick is what
; sets. Else the lead whose own count and the count it calls for, with the
; trick, set the bid, even past a double (Hand 28 trick 4: the 5-4, calling
; the 5-5 for eleven, over the 1-1 calling the 4-1; Hand 31 trick 5: the 4-1,
; for fifteen with the 6-4, over the 4-4's ten). Else a double whose suit
; still has count out; else a tile that calls for count, not a low tile that
; calls for a five, and, against 35 or more, not a low four, five or six,
; which may run into the bidder's doubles (think twice: they come next). Once
; his side has a trick he keeps going for count, set or not: first a count
; tile that calls for more (Hand 28 trick 5, after the set: the 4-1 for
; fifteen with the 6-4, over the 4-4's ten), and last a count tile itself.
; A lead that calls for count also makes the bidder trump rather than throw
; another off cheaply (p. 46): after Hand 32's set the right setter leads the
; 5-4 for that (S-0143-b).
; Replaces gates/c15-setter-leads-call-for-count.silas and
; gates/c13d-lead-a-singleton.silas. How it differs: the C15 gate leads past
; the count that sets to its count-calling double (Hands 28 and 31); its
; one-point exception leads any no-count tile and only when nothing calls for
; count, where the book leads a double (S-0070-c); it has no 35+ caution
; (S-0069-d) and no count-tile lead (S-0067-c). C13d has no page; its one
; instance is Hand 28 trick 4, where the book leads the count that sets, and
; it is not encoded. Double-dummy, the gate's 1-1 is the better defence in
; Hand 28 (19 to the book's 25) and the 4-4 equal in Hand 31 (S-0130-f,
; S-0140-b): the book counts one trick; this file follows the book.
; "What sets" sums one called tile with the lead's own count and the trick,
; against what the setters still need: six literal sums (prelude, lead-sets).

(include book)

(policy setter-leads
  (rule one-point-sets-lead-a-double (play lead)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (on-lead me)
    (to-set 1)
    (own-legal lead)
    (double lead))
  (rule lead-the-count-that-sets (play lead)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (on-lead me)
    (own-legal lead)
    (lead-sets lead))
  (rule lead-count-that-calls-for-more (play lead)
    (pattern
      (viewer me)
      (setter me)
      (on-lead me)
      (not (banked me 0))
      (own-legal lead)
      (count lead 5)
      (calls-for lead 10))
    (pattern
      (viewer me)
      (setter me)
      (on-lead me)
      (not (banked me 0))
      (own-legal lead)
      (count lead 10)
      (calls-for-count lead)))
  (rule a-double-that-calls-for-count (play lead)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (on-lead me)
    (own-legal lead)
    (double lead)
    (calls-for-count lead))
  (rule a-tile-that-calls-for-count (play lead)
    (pattern
      (viewer me)
      (setter me)
      (on-lead me)
      (own-legal lead)
      (not (double lead))
      (calls-for-count lead)
      (not (can-lose lead)))
    (pattern
      (viewer me)
      (setter me)
      (on-lead me)
      (own-legal lead)
      (not (double lead))
      (calls-for-count lead)
      (not (calls-for lead 5))
      (or (not (bid-35-or-more)) (not (low-four-five-or-six lead)))))
  (rule think-twice-a-low-four-five-or-six (play lead)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (on-lead me)
    (own-legal lead)
    (not (double lead))
    (calls-for-count lead)
    (not (calls-for lead 5)))
  (rule lead-a-count-tile (play lead)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (on-lead me)
    (not (banked me 0))
    (own-legal lead)
    (count-tile lead)))
